        "At the beginning of July, on a stiflingly hot evening, a young man left the tiny room he rented from tenants in S. Lane and walked slowly, as if undecided, toward K. Bridge.",
        "He had been lucky enough to avoid his landlady on the stairs. His room was right under the roof of a tall five-story building and was more like a cupboard than a room. The landlady, who gave him his meals and tidied his room, lived one floor below; her kitchen door always stood open onto the staircase. Every time he went out, the young man had to pass that door, and every time he passed it he was gripped by a sick, cowering dread mixed with shame. He owed her a good deal of money and was terrified of running into her.",
        "He was not timid or downtrodden by nature; quite the opposite. But for some time he had been tense and irritable, in a state that resembled a dark melancholy. He had withdrawn so far into himself, cut himself off so completely from everyone, that he shrank from meeting anyone at all, not only his landlady. Poverty was crushing him; and yet lately he had stopped feeling even that. He had given up his everyday affairs; he no longer wanted to deal with them.",
        "“I want to try a thing like that, and I am afraid of these trifles!” he thought with an odd smile. “Everything is in a man’s hands, and he lets it all slip away out of sheer cowardice. What are people most afraid of? A new step, a new word of their own. But I talk too much. I do nothing because I talk; or perhaps I talk because I do nothing. And why am I going there now? Am I really capable of that? Is it serious? Not at all. A fantasy to amuse myself, a toy!”",
        "The heat in the street was terrible. The crowds, the scaffolding going up everywhere, the lime, the bricks, the dust, and that particular smell known to everyone who cannot escape the city in summer, all strained his already frayed nerves. The heavy reek of the taverns, so many in that part of town, and the drunkards one met even during working hours completed the gloom of the scene. For a moment a look of deep disgust crossed the young man’s fine features. He was remarkably handsome, with beautiful dark eyes and dark brown hair, taller than average, slim and well built. But soon he sank into deep thought and walked on without seeing anything around him.",
